=== scenario E: a registered remote with no served certificate refuses admission instead of counting it free
-- an otherwise free pool, but the registered remote has never been served
fleet-seats: no seat - remote secondmate(s) mate2 have not confirmed the current seat policy, so their agents cannot be counted yet (a pooled model is never launched without a counted seat; choose another route or repair the authority)
exit=5

-- the operator removes the unreachable remote registration
fleet-seats: reserved pool=pa id=free-task generation=g-free used=1 capacity=1
exit=0


=== scenario F: generation transitions free exactly the released seat
-- released generation, then a retry of that same terminal generation
fleet-seats: released id=free-task generation=g-free reason=teardown
release exit=0
fleet-seats: refused - generation g-free of free-task is already terminal; a new episode needs a new generation
terminal-generation retry exit=5

-- a successor generation on the same holder is admitted on the freed seat
fleet-seats: reserved pool=pa id=free-task generation=g2 used=1 capacity=1
successor exit=0

-- holder record after the transitions
{"task":"free-task","incarnations":[{"generation":"g-free","previous_generation":null,"lifecycle":"released"},{"generation":"g2","previous_generation":"g-free","lifecycle":"reserved"}]}
